#!/bin/sh
# ucode-analyzer, run in its container image: put this script on your PATH and
# use it as the command itself, from an editor (`ucode-analyzer server`) or a
# shell or CI job (`ucode-analyzer lint`).
#
# The workspace and the current directory are mounted at their own paths, so
# the file locations the server reports are valid here; files elsewhere are
# not visible to it. The user config directory (--config, default
# ~/.config/ucode-analyzer) is mounted read-only. It runs as you, without
# network access.
#
#   UCODE_ANALYZER_IMAGE    the image (default: the release this script is from)
#   UCODE_ANALYZER_RUNTIME  docker or podman (default: whichever is installed)

set -eu

VERSION=0.1.0
IMAGE="${UCODE_ANALYZER_IMAGE:-ghcr.io/m00qek/ucode-analyzer:${VERSION}}"

RUNTIME="${UCODE_ANALYZER_RUNTIME:-}"
if [ -z "${RUNTIME}" ]; then
	if command -v docker >/dev/null 2>&1; then
		RUNTIME=docker
	elif command -v podman >/dev/null 2>&1; then
		RUNTIME=podman
	else
		echo 'ucode-analyzer: docker or podman is needed to run it' >&2
		exit 2
	fi
fi

# The value of option $1 (`--opt=v` or `--opt v`) among the remaining
# arguments, or nothing.
option() {
	name=$1
	shift
	while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
		case "$1" in
			"${name}="*) printf '%s' "${1#*=}"; return ;;
			"${name}") [ $# -gt 1 ] && printf '%s' "$2"; return ;;
		esac
		shift
	done
}

HERE=$(pwd -P)
WORKSPACE=$(option --workspace "$@")
CONFIG=$(option --config "$@")

# `server` (also the default subcommand) needs both; fill in what is missing.
case "${1:-server}" in
	-*|server)
		if [ -z "${CONFIG}" ]; then
			CONFIG="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-${HOME}/.config}/ucode-analyzer"
			mkdir -p "${CONFIG}"
			set -- "$@" --config "${CONFIG}"
		fi
		if [ -z "${WORKSPACE}" ]; then
			WORKSPACE=${HERE}
			set -- "$@" --workspace "${WORKSPACE}"
		fi
		;;
esac

# The command, built backwards in front of the arguments to pass on.
set -- "${IMAGE}" "$@"
set -- -w "${HERE}" "$@"
if [ -n "${CONFIG}" ] && [ -d "${CONFIG}" ]; then
	CONFIG=$(cd "${CONFIG}" && pwd -P)
	set -- -v "${CONFIG}:${CONFIG}:ro" "$@"
fi
if [ -n "${WORKSPACE}" ]; then
	WORKSPACE=$(cd "${WORKSPACE}" && pwd -P)
	set -- -v "${WORKSPACE}:${WORKSPACE}" "$@"
fi
case "${HERE}/" in
	"${WORKSPACE:-//}/"*) ;;
	*) set -- -v "${HERE}:${HERE}" "$@" ;;
esac
# Files it writes (`lint --init`) belong to you.
if [ "${RUNTIME}" = podman ]; then
	set -- --userns=keep-id "$@"
else
	set -- --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" "$@"
fi
exec "${RUNTIME}" run --rm -i --init --network none "$@"
